serial: pl01x: bind the Raspberry Pi 5 debug UART ("arm,pl011-axi")

The firmware device tree describes the Raspberry Pi 5 debug UART (UART10,
the three-pin JST-SH connector) as "arm,pl011-axi" only. The PL011 driver
matched "arm,pl011" and "arm,pl010", so no serial driver was bound and
U-Boot started with no console at all (no banner, no "U-Boot>" prompt).

Match "arm,pl011-axi" as a PL011. The firmware has already configured this
UART at 115200 8N1 (it prints its own log and BL31's on it), so skip the
line setup as with the "skip-init" property.

---
--- a/drivers/serial/serial_pl01x.c
+++ b/drivers/serial/serial_pl01x.c
@@ -370,6 +370,7 @@
 #if CONFIG_IS_ENABLED(OF_REAL)
 static const struct udevice_id pl01x_serial_id[] ={
 	{.compatible = "arm,pl011", .data = TYPE_PL011},
+	{.compatible = "arm,pl011-axi", .data = TYPE_PL011},
 	{.compatible = "arm,pl010", .data = TYPE_PL010},
 	{}
 };
@@ -408,6 +409,10 @@
 	}
 	plat->type = dev_get_driver_data(dev);
 	plat->skip_init = dev_read_bool(dev, "skip-init");
+	/* Raspberry Pi 5: debug UART (UART10) is already set up by the firmware at 115200,
+	 * so only bind the driver and do not touch the line settings. */
+	if (device_is_compatible(dev, "arm,pl011-axi"))
+		plat->skip_init = true;
 
 	return 0;
 }
